  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-sectoral response to population movement in Tigray and Contested Area 2 and multi-purpose cash assistance to support food security in Oromia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia continues to face a complex humanitarian situation characterized by ongoing conflict, climate-related shocks, and localized violence, resulting in both new displacements and increased humanitarian needs among existing internally displaced populations with limited prospects for return. To respond to these needs in Tigray and Contested Area 2, IOM is delivering an integrated response including emergency shelter assistance, site coordination and management support integrated with lifesaving health and nutrition services, protection and mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) services, and targeted water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) interventions to improve living conditions and reduce protection risks for crisis-affected populations. In parallel, in Oromia region, through multi-purpose cash assistance (MPCA), IOM is targeting non-displaced people experiencing extreme acute food insecurity, critical livelihood coping strategies, and/or extreme levels of acute malnutrition.</narrative>
  </description>
